@           Configuration Editor (Logical Address Editor SubMenu)
           -----------------------------------------------------

Use this editor to modify the logical address configuration
information.

Field Description:
------------------
1. Logical Address:
                    Logical Address of the VXIcpu-030. Valid values are
                    0 - 255. 255 establishes the VXIcpu-030 as a dynamic device.
2. Device Type:
                    Device Type for the VXIcpu-030. The different choices
                    are Extended (1), Message Based (2), or Register
                    Based (3) device.
3. Address Space:
                    Address space for slave accesses to VXIcpu-030. The
                    options are A16 only (3), A16/A24 (0) and A16/A32 (1).
4. Shared RAM:
                    The VXIcpu-030 can be configured for the following
                    slave accesses.
                    Disable(0) - Allow A16 accesses only.
                    A24/A32(1) - Share 2 Mb  of RAM.
                    A24/A32(2) - Share 4 Mb  of RAM.
                    A24/A32(3) - Share 8 Mb  of RAM.
                    A24/A32(4) - Share 16 Mb of RAM.

5. Slave Block Transfer Mode :
                    This is statically configured to 0, i.e., slave
                    block accesses are not supported.
6. Slave Supervisory Access Only :
                    Selecting a value of 1 restricts the slave accesses
                    to be supervisory only. When 0 is selected, both
                    unprivileged and supervisory slave accesses succeed.
7. Resource Manager Delay (sec) :
                    This gives the time in seconds that the
                    Resource Manager waits for sysfail to be
                    removed in the system before starting to
                    configure the devices.
8. Servant Area Size:
                     This gives the slave area size if the VXIcpu-030
                     is configured to be a Message Based device and
                     has servants.
9. Protocol Register:
                     This gives the Protocol Register value which
                     defines the supported protocols.
10.Read Protocol Response:
                     This gives the response value to a Read Protocol
                     query received by the VXIcpu-030 as a Message Based
                     device.
11.Number of Handlers:
                     This gives the number of handlers for the
                     VXIcpu-030.
12.Number of Interrupters:
                     This gives the number of interrupters for the
                     VXIcpu-030.
13.Cmdr WS Poll Value:
                     This gives the relative time to wait in a loop
                     before sleeping in the kernel in a Word Serial
                     call when polling for Write Ready or Read Ready.

Usage
-----
It supports the following commands:

(1) list      [<index#>,[<index#>]] - lists all the entries in the
                                      specified range.
(2) display   [<index#>,[<index#>]] - displays the entries in detail.
(3) modify    <index#>              - lets you modify an existing entry.
(4) save                            - lets you save the information.
(5) abort                           - lets you exit the editor,
                                      ignoring the changes made.
(6) exit                            - lets you exit the editor.
(7) help                            - gives help on that editor.
